# What never belongs in a build context.
#
# All three services now build from the project root — they install the whole
# workspace so the dependency resolution matches what the application was
# generated against. That makes the context the entire project, and without this
# file every `docker compose build` would upload `node_modules` and `.git` to the
# daemon before running a single instruction. On a generated app that is hundreds
# of megabytes and several seconds, every build.
#
# Dependencies are installed *inside* the image from `package.json`, so a host
# `node_modules` is not merely wasteful — it is the wrong platform's binaries.
node_modules
**/node_modules
.git
.gitignore

# Build output. Regenerated in the image; a stale copy shadows it.
dist
**/dist
.output
**/.output
.vinxi
**/.vinxi
.nitro
**/.nitro
build
**/build

# Local state and secrets. `.env` in particular: compose passes configuration as
# environment variables, and baking a developer's keys into an image layer is
# how they end up in a registry.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
*.log
.DS_Store
.vscode
.idea

# Test and coverage artifacts
coverage
**/coverage
test-results
playwright-report
